  "summary": "Oak Park trustee Derek Eder explains his Aug. 5 vote with a 5-2 board majority to cancel the village's Flock Safety contract and deactivate 8 ALPR cameras. He cites data-sharing with ICE, CBP, and Texas abortion enforcement, lack of effectiveness data, and broader surveillance concerns.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "I voted along with the 5-2 majority on the Oak Park Village Board to cancel our contract with Flock Safety and deactivate the 8 Automatic License Plate Reader (ALPR) cameras",
